IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa28-part46`

-- coa28-sch1b.l4: Schedule 1B (Enforcement of disclosure requirements), paragraphs 1 to 14B,
-- lines 18810-18945 of ukpga-2006-46.txt (a plain-text rendering from legislation.gov.uk; not the official text).
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Schedule 1B is what a company may do when a person does not answer a notice under
-- ss 790D, 790DA, 790E or 790EA (coa17): a warning notice, a restrictions notice, its effects, the court's powers
-- over it, and the offences. The notices and duties named here are taken as plain facts; the officer-in-default
-- test of s 1121 (coa24) is taken as an input named for that section.
-- Answers are MAYBE BOOLEAN: JUST FALSE only where the text says no in its own words (FALSE-kind comments), NOTHING
-- otherwise (NOTHING-kind comments). "must not ... unless" is a BAR function: JUST TRUE when the bar holds.
-- A penalty is a `Penalty` of coa-core.l4, or NOTHING where the text gives none for the mode of conviction asked.

-- =========================================================================================================
-- Right to issue a restrictions notice (paragraph 1)
-- =========================================================================================================

-- src:18813 | 1 (1) This paragraph applies if—
-- src:18814 | (a) a notice under section 790D , 790DA, 790E or 790EA is served by a company on a person who has a relevant interest in the company, and
-- src:18815 | (b) the person fails to comply with that notice within the time specified in it.
@ref sch 1B para 1(1) Right to issue restrictions notice (src:18813-18815)
GIVEN `a notice under section 790D, 790DA, 790E or 790EA is served by a company on a person who has a relevant interest in the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person fails to comply with that notice within the time specified in it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1B para 1(1) paragraph 1 applies` MEANS
    IF `a notice under section 790D, 790DA, 790E or 790EA is served by a company on a person who has a relevant interest in the company` AND `the person fails to comply with that notice within the time specified in it`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This paragraph applies if" (a) and (b) (a failed "if": marginal reading M1 in NOTES.md)

-- src:18816 | (2) The company may give the person a notice under this paragraph (a “warning notice”) informing the person that it is proposing to issue the person with a notice (a “restrictions notice”) with respect to the relevant interest.
@ref sch 1B para 1(2) Right to issue restrictions notice (src:18816)
GIVEN `paragraph 1 applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1B para 1(2) the company may give the person a warning notice` MEANS
    CONSIDER `paragraph 1 applies`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The company may give the person a notice" follows "This paragraph applies if"; when the paragraph does not apply, a function named for a power does not read the failed "if" as "may not" (fork F11 in NOTES.md; RECONCILED 2026-11-12, was JUST FALSE)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether paragraph 1 applies is not answered

-- "the period of one month beginning with the date": counted from the date as day 1, it ends on the day before the
-- same day of the next month, or on the last day of the next month if that month is shorter (fork F6 in NOTES.md).
-- src:18817 | (3) The company may issue the restrictions notice if, by the end of the period of one month beginning with the date on which the warning notice was given—
@ref sch 1B para 1(3) Right to issue restrictions notice (src:18817)
GIVEN `the date on which the warning notice was given` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`sch 1B para 1(3) the last day of the period of one month beginning with the date on which the warning notice was given` MEANS
    IF DATE_DAY `the date on which the warning notice was given` EQUALS 1
    THEN Date (`Days in month` (DATE_MONTH `the date on which the warning notice was given`) (DATE_YEAR `the date on which the warning notice was given`)) (DATE_MONTH `the date on which the warning notice was given`) (DATE_YEAR `the date on which the warning notice was given`)
    ELSE Date (min (DATE_DAY `the date on which the warning notice was given` MINUS 1) (`Days in month` nextMonth nextYear)) nextMonth nextYear
    WHERE
        nextMonth MEANS IF DATE_MONTH `the date on which the warning notice was given` EQUALS 12 THEN 1 ELSE DATE_MONTH `the date on which the warning notice was given` PLUS 1
        nextYear MEANS IF DATE_MONTH `the date on which the warning notice was given` EQUALS 12 THEN DATE_YEAR `the date on which the warning notice was given` PLUS 1 ELSE DATE_YEAR `the date on which the warning notice was given`

-- src:18817 | (3) The company may issue the restrictions notice if, by the end of the period of one month beginning with the date on which the warning notice was given—
-- src:18818 | (a) the person has not complied with the notice served under section 790D , 790DA, 790E or 790EA, and
-- src:18819 | (b) the company has not been provided with a valid reason sufficient to justify the person's failure to comply with the notice served under that section.
@ref sch 1B para 1(3) Right to issue restrictions notice (src:18817-18819)
GIVEN `the date on which the warning notice was given` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the company wishes to issue the restrictions notice` IS A DATE
      `by the end of that period the person has not complied with the notice served under section 790D, 790DA, 790E or 790EA` IS A BOOLEAN
      `by the end of that period the company has not been provided with a valid reason sufficient to justify the person's failure to comply` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1B para 1(3) the company may issue the restrictions notice` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the day on which the company wishes to issue the restrictions notice` AT MOST `sch 1B para 1(3) the last day of the period of one month beginning with the date on which the warning notice was given` `the date on which the warning notice was given`
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may issue the restrictions notice if, by the end of the period of one month beginning with the date on which the warning notice was given" (the period has not ended)
        IF `by the end of that period the person has not complied with the notice served under section 790D, 790DA, 790E or 790EA` AND `by the end of that period the company has not been provided with a valid reason sufficient to justify the person's failure to comply`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if, by the end of the period of one month ..., (a) the person has not complied ..., and (b) the company has not been provided with a valid reason" (a failed "if")

-- src:18820 | (4) A restrictions notice is issued on a person by sending the notice to the person.
@ref sch 1B para 1(4) Right to issue restrictions notice (src:18820)
GIVEN `the notice has been sent to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1B para 1(4) the restrictions notice is issued on the person` MEANS
    IF `the notice has been sent to the person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A restrictions notice is issued on a person by sending the notice to the person"

-- src:18822 | (6) In deciding whether to issue a restrictions notice, the company must have regard to the effect of the notice on the rights of third parties in respect of the relevant interest.
@ref sch 1B para 1(6) Right to issue restrictions notice (src:18822)
GIVEN `the company has had regard to the effect of the notice on the rights of third parties in respect of the relevant interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1B para 1(6) the company has had regard to the effect of the notice on the rights of third parties` MEANS
    IF `the company has had regard to the effect of the notice on the rights of third parties in respect of the relevant interest`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the company must have regard to the effect of the notice on the rights of third parties" (a bare "must" not done: fork F3)

-- The same duty as a regulative rule: the company (a party the core names) must have regard to the effect of the notice
-- on third parties' rights in deciding whether to issue it. The text gives no time limit and no consequence, so the rule has neither.
DECLARE `sch 1B para 1(6) action` IS ONE OF
    `sch 1B para 1(6) the company has regard to the effect of the notice on the rights of third parties`

GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `sch 1B para 1(6) action`
`sch 1B para 1(6) the company's duty to have regard to the rights of third parties` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `sch 1B para 1(6) the company has regard to the effect of the notice on the rights of third parties`

-- =========================================================================================================
-- Relevant interests (paragraph 2)
-- =========================================================================================================

-- src:18824 | 2 (1) For the purposes of this Schedule, a person has a relevant interest in a company if the person—
-- src:18825 | (a) holds any shares in the company,
-- src:18826 | (b) holds any voting rights in the company, or
-- src:18827 | (c) holds the right to appoint or remove any member of the board of directors of the company.
@ref sch 1B para 2(1) Relevant interests (src:18824-18827)
GIVEN `the person holds any shares in the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person holds any voting rights in the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person holds the right to appoint or remove any member of the board of directors of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1B para 2(1) the person has a relevant interest in the company` MEANS
    IF `the person holds any shares in the company` OR `the person holds any voting rights in the company` OR `the person holds the right to appoint or remove any member of the board of directors of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person has a relevant interest in a company if the person— (a) holds any shares in the company, (b) holds any voting rights in the company, or (c) holds the right to appoint or remove any member of the board" (a failed "if": marginal reading M1)

-- src:18828 | (2) References to “the relevant interest” are to the shares or right in question.
@ref sch 1B para 2(2) Relevant interests (src:18828)
GIVEN `the thing is the shares or right in question` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1B para 2(2) the thing is the relevant interest` MEANS
    IF `the thing is the shares or right in question`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "References to “the relevant interest” are to the shares or right in question"

-- src:18829 | (3) Part 3 of Schedule 1A applies for the interpretation of sub-paragraph (1) save that, where the relevant interest is by virtue of paragraph 19 or 20 of that Schedule treated for the purposes of that Schedule as held by a person other than the person who in fact holds the interest, both the holder and the other person are to be regarded for the purposes of this Schedule as having the relevant interest.
@ref sch 1B para 2(3) Relevant interests (src:18829)
GIVEN `the relevant interest is by virtue of paragraph 19 or 20 of Schedule 1A treated as held by a person other than the person who in fact holds the interest` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person asked about is the person who in fact holds the interest, or the other person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1B para 2(3) the person is regarded as having the relevant interest` MEANS
    IF `the relevant interest is by virtue of paragraph 19 or 20 of Schedule 1A treated as held by a person other than the person who in fact holds the interest` AND `the person asked about is the person who in fact holds the interest, or the other person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "where the relevant interest is by virtue of paragraph 19 or 20 of that Schedule treated ... as held by a person other than the person who in fact holds the interest, both the holder and the other person are to be regarded"

-- =========================================================================================================
-- Effect of restrictions notice (paragraph 3)
-- =========================================================================================================

-- src:18843 | (7) The provisions of this section are subject to any directions given under paragraph 4.
@ref sch 1B para 3(7) Effect of restrictions notice (src:18843)
GIVEN `a direction under paragraph 4 covers the act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1B para 3(7) the provisions of paragraph 3 are subject to the direction` MEANS
    IF `a direction under paragraph 4 covers the act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "subject to any directions given under paragraph 4"

DECLARE `sch 1B para 3(1) act` IS ONE OF
    `sch 1B para 3(1)(a) a transfer of the interest`
    `sch 1B para 3(1)(b) the exercise of a right in respect of the interest`
    `sch 1B para 3(1)(c) the issue of shares in right of the interest or in pursuance of an offer made to the interest-holder`
    `sch 1B para 3(1)(d) a payment of sums due from the company in respect of the interest, whether in respect of capital or otherwise`
    `sch 1B para 3(1) another act`

-- src:18831 | 3 (1) The effect of a restrictions notice issued under paragraph 1 with respect to a relevant interest is as follows—
-- src:18832 | (a) any transfer of the interest is void,
-- src:18833 | (b) no rights are exercisable in respect of the interest,
-- src:18834 | (c) no shares may be issued in right of the interest or in pursuance of an offer made to the interest-holder,
-- src:18835 | (d) except in a liquidation, no payment may be made of sums due from the company in respect of the interest, whether in respect of capital or otherwise.
@ref sch 1B para 3(1) Effect of restrictions notice (src:18831-18835)
GIVEN act IS A `sch 1B para 3(1) act`
      `a restrictions notice issued under paragraph 1 is in force with respect to the interest` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is in a liquidation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provisions of paragraph 3 are subject to the direction` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1B para 3(1) the effect of the restrictions notice applies to the act` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`a restrictions notice issued under paragraph 1 is in force with respect to the interest`)
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The effect of a restrictions notice issued under paragraph 1 with respect to a relevant interest is as follows"
        IF act EQUALS `sch 1B para 3(1) another act`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the effects in (a) to (d) are not closed with "only"
        IF `the provisions of paragraph 3 are subject to the direction` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The provisions of this section are subject to any directions given under paragraph 4" (fork F7: the other reading is that a covered act is not restricted)
        IF act EQUALS `sch 1B para 3(1)(d) a payment of sums due from the company in respect of the interest, whether in respect of capital or otherwise` AND `the company is in a liquidation`
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(d) except in a liquidation, no payment may be made of sums due from the company in respect of the interest"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:18840 | (6) An “ associated right ”, in relation to a relevant interest, is—
-- src:18841 | (a) a right to be issued with any shares issued in right of the relevant interest, or
-- src:18842 | (b) a right to receive payment of any sums due from the company in respect of the relevant interest.
@ref sch 1B para 3(6) Effect of restrictions notice (src:18840-18842)
GIVEN `the right is a right to be issued with any shares issued in right of the relevant interest` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the right is a right to receive payment of any sums due from the company in respect of the relevant interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1B para 3(6) the right is an associated right in relation to the relevant interest` MEANS
    IF `the right is a right to be issued with any shares issued in right of the relevant interest` OR `the right is a right to receive payment of any sums due from the company in respect of the relevant interest`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An “associated right”, in relation to a relevant interest, is— (a) a right to be issued with any shares issued in right of the relevant interest, or (b) a right to receive payment of any sums due" (a quoted-term definition read as closed: marginal reading M2)

-- src:18837 | (3) Sub-paragraph (2) does not apply to an agreement to transfer the interest on the making of an order under paragraph 8 made by virtue of sub-paragraph (3)(b) of that paragraph (removal of restrictions in case of court-approved transfer).
@ref sch 1B para 3(3) Effect of restrictions notice (src:18837)
GIVEN `the agreement is to transfer the interest on the making of an order under paragraph 8 made by virtue of sub-paragraph (3)(b) of that paragraph` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1B para 3(3) sub-paragraph (2) applies to the agreement` MEANS
    IF `the agreement is to transfer the interest on the making of an order under paragraph 8 made by virtue of sub-paragraph (3)(b) of that paragraph`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Sub-paragraph (2) does not apply to an agreement to transfer the interest on the making of an order under paragraph 8 made by virtue of sub-paragraph (3)(b)"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sub-paragraph says only where (2) does not apply

-- src:18836 | (2) An agreement to transfer an interest that is subject to the restriction in sub-paragraph (1)(a) is void.
@ref sch 1B para 3(2) Effect of restrictions notice (src:18836)
GIVEN `the interest is subject to the restriction in sub-paragraph (1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `sub-paragraph (2) applies to the agreement` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1B para 3(2) the agreement to transfer the interest is void` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `sub-paragraph (2) applies to the agreement` EQUALS JUST FALSE
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Sub-paragraph (2) does not apply to an agreement to transfer the interest on the making of an order under paragraph 8" (sub-paragraph (3))
        IF `the interest is subject to the restriction in sub-paragraph (1)(a)`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An agreement to transfer an interest that is subject to the restriction in sub-paragraph (1)(a)"

-- src:18839 | (5) Sub-paragraph (4) does not apply to an agreement to transfer any such right on the making of an order under paragraph 8 made by virtue of sub-paragraph (3)(b) of that paragraph (removal of restrictions in case of court-approved transfer).
@ref sch 1B para 3(5) Effect of restrictions notice (src:18839)
GIVEN `the agreement is to transfer the associated right on the making of an order under paragraph 8 made by virtue of sub-paragraph (3)(b) of that paragraph` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1B para 3(5) sub-paragraph (4) applies to the agreement` MEANS
    IF `the agreement is to transfer the associated right on the making of an order under paragraph 8 made by virtue of sub-paragraph (3)(b) of that paragraph`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Sub-paragraph (4) does not apply to an agreement to transfer any such right on the making of an order under paragraph 8 made by virtue of sub-paragraph (3)(b)"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sub-paragraph says only where (4) does not apply

-- src:18838 | (4) An agreement to transfer any associated right (otherwise than in a liquidation) is void.
@ref sch 1B para 3(4) Effect of restrictions notice (src:18838)
GIVEN `the agreement is to transfer an associated right` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transfer is in a liquidation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `sub-paragraph (4) applies to the agreement` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1B para 3(4) the agreement to transfer the associated right is void` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `sub-paragraph (4) applies to the agreement` EQUALS JUST FALSE
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Sub-paragraph (4) does not apply to an agreement to transfer any such right on the making of an order under paragraph 8" (sub-paragraph (5))
        IF `the transfer is in a liquidation`
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An agreement to transfer any associated right (otherwise than in a liquidation) is void"
        IF `the agreement is to transfer an associated right`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An agreement to transfer any associated right"

-- =========================================================================================================
-- Protection of third party rights (paragraph 4)
-- =========================================================================================================

-- src:18845 | 4 (1) The court may give a direction under this paragraph if, on application by any person aggrieved, the court is satisfied that a restrictions notice issued by the company under paragraph 1 unfairly affects the rights of third parties in respect of the relevant interest.
@ref sch 1B para 4(1) Protection of third party rights (src:18845)
GIVEN `an application is made by a person aggrieved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that a restrictions notice issued by the company under paragraph 1 unfairly affects the rights of third parties in respect of the relevant interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1B para 4(1) the court may give a direction` MEANS
    IF `an application is made by a person aggrieved` AND `the court is satisfied that a restrictions notice issued by the company under paragraph 1 unfairly affects the rights of third parties in respect of the relevant interest`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The court may give a direction under this paragraph if, on application by any person aggrieved, the court is satisfied that a restrictions notice ... unfairly affects the rights of third parties", not "only if": a function named for a power does not read the failed "if" as "may not" (fork F12 in NOTES.md; RECONCILED 2026-11-12, was JUST FALSE)

-- src:18847 | (3) The direction is a direction that certain acts will not constitute a breach of the restrictions placed on the relevant interest by the restrictions notice.
@ref sch 1B para 4(3) Protection of third party rights (src:18847)
GIVEN `the court has given a direction under paragraph 4 that covers the act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1B para 4(3) the act does not constitute a breach of the restrictions placed on the relevant interest` MEANS
    IF `the court has given a direction under paragraph 4 that covers the act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a direction that certain acts will not constitute a breach of the restrictions"

-- src:18848 | (4) An order containing a direction under this paragraph—
-- src:18849 | (a) must specify the acts that will not constitute a breach of the restrictions, and
@ref sch 1B para 4(4)(a) Protection of third party rights (src:18848-18849)
GIVEN `the order containing the direction specifies the acts that will not constitute a breach of the restrictions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1B para 4(4)(a) the order containing the direction meets the requirement to specify the acts` MEANS
    IF `the order containing the direction specifies the acts that will not constitute a breach of the restrictions`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An order containing a direction under this paragraph— (a) must specify the acts that will not constitute a breach of the restrictions" (a bare "must" not done: fork F3)

-- src:18848 | (4) An order containing a direction under this paragraph—
-- src:18850 | (b) may confine the direction to cases where those acts are done by persons, or for purposes, described in the order.
@ref sch 1B para 4(4)(b) Protection of third party rights (src:18848 and src:18850)
GIVEN `the direction is confined to cases where those acts are done by persons, or for purposes, described in the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1B para 4(4)(b) the order may confine the direction to cases where the acts are done by persons or for purposes described in the order` MEANS
    IF `the direction is confined to cases where those acts are done by persons, or for purposes, described in the order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may confine the direction to cases where those acts are done by persons, or for purposes, described in the order"

-- src:18851 | (5) The direction may be given subject to such terms as the court thinks fit.
@ref sch 1B para 4(5) Protection of third party rights (src:18851)
GIVEN `the court thinks the terms fit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1B para 4(5) the direction may be given subject to the terms` MEANS
    IF `the court thinks the terms fit`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "subject to such terms as the court thinks fit"

-- =========================================================================================================
-- Breach of restrictions: the offences (paragraphs 5 and 6) and their penalties (paragraph 7)
-- =========================================================================================================

-- src:18874 | (2) The provisions of those paragraphs are subject to any direction given under paragraph 4 or 8.
@ref sch 1B para 7(2) Breach of restrictions (src:18874)
GIVEN `an order under paragraph 4 or 8 contains a direction that covers the act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1B para 7(2) the provisions of paragraphs 5 and 6 are subject to the direction` MEANS
    IF `an order under paragraph 4 or 8 contains a direction that covers the act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "subject to any direction given under paragraph 4 or 8"

DECLARE `sch 1B para 5(2) thing` IS ONE OF
    `sch 1B para 5(2)(a) exercising or purporting to exercise any right to dispose of a relevant interest`
    `sch 1B para 5(2)(b) exercising or purporting to exercise any right to dispose of any right to be issued with a relevant interest`
    `sch 1B para 5(2)(c) voting in respect of a relevant interest (whether as holder of the interest or as proxy) or appointing a proxy to vote in respect of a relevant interest`
    `sch 1B para 5(2) another thing`

-- src:18853 | 5 (1) A person commits an offence if the person does anything listed in sub-paragraph (2) knowing that the interest is subject to restrictions.
-- src:18854 | (2) The things are—
-- src:18855 | (a) exercising or purporting to exercise any right to dispose of a relevant interest,
-- src:18856 | (b) exercising or purporting to exercise any right to dispose of any right to be issued with a relevant interest, or
-- src:18857 | (c) voting in respect of a relevant interest (whether as holder of the interest or as proxy) or appointing a proxy to vote in respect of a relevant interest.
@ref sch 1B para 5(1) Breach of restrictions (src:18853-18857)
GIVEN thing IS A `sch 1B para 5(2) thing`
      `the person knows that the interest is subject to restrictions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provisions of paragraphs 5 and 6 are subject to the direction` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1B para 5(1) the person commits an offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the provisions of paragraphs 5 and 6 are subject to the direction` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The provisions of those paragraphs are subject to any direction given under paragraph 4 or 8" (fork F7)
        IF thing EQUALS `sch 1B para 5(2) another thing`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "The things are" (a) to (c), not closed with "only"
        IF `the person knows that the interest is subject to restrictions`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person commits an offence if the person does anything listed in sub-paragraph (2) knowing that the interest is subject to restrictions" (a failed "if": marginal reading M1)

-- src:18858 | (3) A person who has a relevant interest that the person knows to be subject to restrictions commits an offence if the person—
-- src:18859 | (a) knows a person to be entitled (apart from the restrictions) to vote in respect of the interest, whether as holder or as proxy,
-- src:18860 | (b) does not know the person to be aware of the fact that the interest is subject to restrictions, and
-- src:18861 | (c) fails to notify the person of that fact.
@ref sch 1B para 5(3) Breach of restrictions (src:18858-18861)
GIVEN `the person has a relevant interest that the person knows to be subject to restrictions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knows another person to be entitled (apart from the restrictions) to vote in respect of the interest, whether as holder or as proxy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person does not know the other person to be aware of the fact that the interest is subject to restrictions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person fails to notify the other person of that fact` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provisions of paragraphs 5 and 6 are subject to the direction` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1B para 5(3) the person commits an offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the provisions of paragraphs 5 and 6 are subject to the direction` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The provisions of those paragraphs are subject to any direction given under paragraph 4 or 8" (fork F7)
        IF       `the person has a relevant interest that the person knows to be subject to restrictions`
             AND `the person knows another person to be entitled (apart from the restrictions) to vote in respect of the interest, whether as holder or as proxy`
             AND `the person does not know the other person to be aware of the fact that the interest is subject to restrictions`
             AND `the person fails to notify the other person of that fact`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person who has a relevant interest that the person knows to be subject to restrictions commits an offence if the person— (a) knows ..., (b) does not know ..., and (c) fails to notify" (a failed "if": marginal reading M1)

-- src:18862 | (4) A person commits an offence if the person—
-- src:18863 | (a) either has a relevant interest that the person knows to be subject to restrictions or is entitled to an associated right, and
-- src:18864 | (b) enters in that capacity into an agreement that is void by virtue of paragraph 3(2) or (4).
@ref sch 1B para 5(4) Breach of restrictions (src:18862-18864)
GIVEN `the person either has a relevant interest that the person knows to be subject to restrictions or is entitled to an associated right` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person enters in that capacity into an agreement that is void by virtue of paragraph 3(2) or (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provisions of paragraphs 5 and 6 are subject to the direction` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1B para 5(4) the person commits an offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the provisions of paragraphs 5 and 6 are subject to the direction` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The provisions of those paragraphs are subject to any direction given under paragraph 4 or 8" (fork F7)
        IF `the person either has a relevant interest that the person knows to be subject to restrictions or is entitled to an associated right` AND `the person enters in that capacity into an agreement that is void by virtue of paragraph 3(2) or (4)`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person commits an offence if the person— (a) either has a relevant interest that the person knows to be subject to restrictions or is entitled to an associated right, and (b) enters in that capacity into an agreement that is void" (a failed "if": marginal reading M1)

-- src:18865 | (5) References in this Schedule to an interest being “subject to restrictions” are to an interest being subject to restrictions by virtue of a restrictions notice under paragraph 1.
@ref sch 1B para 5(5) Breach of restrictions (src:18865)
GIVEN `the interest is subject to restrictions by virtue of a restrictions notice under paragraph 1` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1B para 5(5) the interest is subject to restrictions` MEANS
    IF `the interest is subject to restrictions by virtue of a restrictions notice under paragraph 1`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "References in this Schedule to an interest being “subject to restrictions” are to an interest being subject to restrictions by virtue of a restrictions notice under paragraph 1"

-- src:18866 | 6 If shares in a company are issued in contravention of a restriction imposed by virtue of a restrictions notice under paragraph 1, an offence is committed by—
-- src:18867 | (a) the company, and
@ref sch 1B para 6(a) Breach of restrictions (src:18866-18867)
GIVEN `shares in a company are issued in contravention of a restriction imposed by virtue of a restrictions notice under paragraph 1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provisions of paragraphs 5 and 6 are subject to the direction` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1B para 6(a) the company commits an offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the provisions of paragraphs 5 and 6 are subject to the direction` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The provisions of those paragraphs are subject to any direction given under paragraph 4 or 8" (fork F7)
        IF `shares in a company are issued in contravention of a restriction imposed by virtue of a restrictions notice under paragraph 1`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If shares in a company are issued in contravention of a restriction imposed by virtue of a restrictions notice under paragraph 1, an offence is committed by— (a) the company" (a failed "if": marginal reading M1)

-- src:18866 | 6 If shares in a company are issued in contravention of a restriction imposed by virtue of a restrictions notice under paragraph 1, an offence is committed by—
-- src:18868 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref sch 1B para 6(b) Breach of restrictions (src:18866 and src:18868)
GIVEN `shares in a company are issued in contravention of a restriction imposed by virtue of a restrictions notice under paragraph 1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the provisions of paragraphs 5 and 6 are subject to the direction` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1B para 6(b) the officer of the company commits an offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the provisions of paragraphs 5 and 6 are subject to the direction` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The provisions of those paragraphs are subject to any direction given under paragraph 4 or 8" (fork F7)
        IF NOT (`shares in a company are issued in contravention of a restriction imposed by virtue of a restrictions notice under paragraph 1`)
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If shares in a company are issued in contravention of a restriction imposed by virtue of a restrictions notice under paragraph 1, an offence is committed by ... (b) every officer of the company who is in default" (a failed "if": marginal reading M1)
        OTHERWISE `s 1121 the officer is in default`

-- ---- paragraph 7(1): the penalty for an offence under paragraph 5 or 6 -----------------------------------------------

-- src:18869 | 7 (1) A person guilty of an offence under paragraph 5 or 6 is liable—
-- src:18870 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to a fine;
-- src:18871 | (b) on summary conviction—
-- src:18872 | (i) in England and Wales, to a fine,
-- src:18873 | (ii) in Scotland or Northern Ireland, to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum.
@ref sch 1B para 7(1) Breach of restrictions (src:18869-18873)
GIVEN `how the person is convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`sch 1B para 7(1) the penalty for an offence under paragraph 5 or 6` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how the person is convicted`
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on conviction on indictment`, NOTHING, JUST `a fine without a stated limit`, NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in England and Wales`, NOTHING, JUST `a fine without a stated limit`, NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Scotland` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Scotland`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph distinguishes England and Wales from Scotland and Northern Ireland on summary conviction

-- =========================================================================================================
-- Relaxation of restrictions (paragraph 8)
-- =========================================================================================================

-- src:18876 | 8 (1) An application may be made to the court for an order directing that the relevant interest cease to be subject to restrictions.
-- src:18877 | (2) An application for an order under this paragraph may be made by the company in question or by any person aggrieved.
@ref sch 1B para 8(1) and (2) Relaxation of restrictions (src:18876-18877)
GIVEN `the person is the company in question` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a person aggrieved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1B para 8(2) the person may apply for an order under paragraph 8` MEANS
    IF `the person is the company in question` OR `the person is a person aggrieved`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may be made by the company in question or by any person aggrieved"

-- "must not make an order ... unless" is a bar: JUST TRUE means the court is barred.
-- src:18878 | (3) The court must not make an order under this paragraph unless—
-- src:18879 | (a) it is satisfied that the information required by the notice served under section 790D , 790DA, 790E or 790EA has been disclosed to the company and no unfair advantage has accrued to any person as a result of the earlier failure to make that disclosure, or
-- src:18880 | (b) the relevant interest is to be transferred for valuable consideration and the court approves the transfer.
@ref sch 1B para 8(3) Relaxation of restrictions (src:18878-18880)
GIVEN `the court is satisfied that the information required by the notice served under section 790D, 790DA, 790E or 790EA has been disclosed to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `no unfair advantage has accrued to any person as a result of the earlier failure to make that disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the relevant interest is to be transferred for valuable consideration and the court approves the transfer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1B para 8(3) the court is barred from making an order under paragraph 8` MEANS
    IF       (`the court is satisfied that the information required by the notice served under section 790D, 790DA, 790E or 790EA has been disclosed to the company` AND `no unfair advantage has accrued to any person as a result of the earlier failure to make that disclosure`)
         OR  `the relevant interest is to be transferred for valuable consideration and the court approves the transfer`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The court must not make an order under this paragraph unless— (a) it is satisfied that the information ... has been disclosed ... and no unfair advantage has accrued ..., or (b) the relevant interest is to be transferred for valuable consideration and the court approves the transfer" (the "unless" is met)
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:18881 | (4) An order under this paragraph made by virtue of sub-paragraph (3)(b) may continue, in whole or in part, the restrictions mentioned in paragraph 3(1)(c) and (d) so far as they relate to a right acquired or offer made before the transfer.
@ref sch 1B para 8(4) Relaxation of restrictions (src:18881)
GIVEN `the order is made by virtue of sub-paragraph (3)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the restriction is one mentioned in paragraph 3(1)(c) or (d)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the restriction relates to a right acquired or offer made before the transfer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1B para 8(4) the order may continue the restriction` MEANS
    IF `the order is made by virtue of sub-paragraph (3)(b)` AND `the restriction is one mentioned in paragraph 3(1)(c) or (d)` AND `the restriction relates to a right acquired or offer made before the transfer`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may continue, in whole or in part, the restrictions mentioned in paragraph 3(1)(c) and (d) so far as they relate to a right acquired or offer made before the transfer"

-- src:18882 | (5) Where any restrictions continue in force under sub-paragraph (4)—
-- src:18883 | (a) an application may be made under this paragraph for an order directing that the relevant interest cease to be subject to those restrictions, and
@ref sch 1B para 8(5)(a) Relaxation of restrictions (src:18882-18883)
GIVEN `restrictions continue in force under sub-paragraph (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1B para 8(5)(a) an application may be made for an order directing that the relevant interest cease to be subject to those restrictions` MEANS
    IF `restrictions continue in force under sub-paragraph (4)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where any restrictions continue in force under sub-paragraph (4)"

-- src:18882 | (5) Where any restrictions continue in force under sub-paragraph (4)—
-- src:18884 | (b) sub-paragraph (3) does not apply in relation to the making of such an order.
@ref sch 1B para 8(5)(b) Relaxation of restrictions (src:18882 and src:18884)
GIVEN `restrictions continue in force under sub-paragraph (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1B para 8(5)(b) sub-paragraph (3) applies to the making of the order` MEANS
    IF `restrictions continue in force under sub-paragraph (4)`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "sub-paragraph (3) does not apply in relation to the making of such an order"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where any restrictions continue in force under sub-paragraph (4)"

-- =========================================================================================================
-- Orders for sale (paragraphs 9 and 10)
-- =========================================================================================================

-- src:18886 | 9 (1) The court may order that the relevant interest subject to restrictions be sold subject to the court's approval as to the sale.
@ref sch 1B para 9(1) Orders for sale (src:18886)
GIVEN `the relevant interest is subject to restrictions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1B para 9(1) the court may order that the relevant interest be sold subject to the court's approval as to the sale` MEANS
    IF `the relevant interest is subject to restrictions`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the relevant interest subject to restrictions"

-- src:18887 | (2) An application for an order under sub-paragraph (1) may only be made by the company in question.
@ref sch 1B para 9(2) Orders for sale (src:18887)
GIVEN `the person is the company in question` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1B para 9(2) the person may apply for an order under sub-paragraph (1)` MEANS
    IF `the person is the company in question`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An application for an order under sub-paragraph (1) may only be made by the company in question"

-- src:18888 | (3) If the court makes an order under this paragraph, it may make such further order relating to the sale or transfer of the interest as it thinks fit.
@ref sch 1B para 9(3) Orders for sale (src:18888)
GIVEN `the court has made an order under paragraph 9` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1B para 9(3) the court may make such further order relating to the sale or transfer of the interest as it thinks fit` MEANS
    IF `the court has made an order under paragraph 9`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the court makes an order under this paragraph, it may make such further order"

-- src:18889 | (4) An application for an order under sub-paragraph (3) may be made—
-- src:18890 | (a) by the company in question,
-- src:18891 | (b) by the person appointed by or in pursuance of the order to effect the sale, or
-- src:18892 | (c) by any person with an interest in the relevant interest.
@ref sch 1B para 9(4) Orders for sale (src:18889-18892)
GIVEN `the person is the company in question` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the person appointed by or in pursuance of the order to effect the sale` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has an interest in the relevant interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1B para 9(4) the person may apply for an order under sub-paragraph (3)` MEANS
    IF `the person is the company in question` OR `the person is the person appointed by or in pursuance of the order to effect the sale` OR `the person has an interest in the relevant interest`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "may be made— (a) by the company in question, (b) by the person appointed ..., or (c) by any person with an interest in the relevant interest", with no "only"

-- src:18893 | (5) On making an order under sub-paragraph (1) or (3), the court may order that the applicant's costs (in Scotland, expenses) be paid out of the proceeds of sale.
@ref sch 1B para 9(5) Orders for sale (src:18893)
GIVEN `the court makes an order under sub-paragraph (1) or (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1B para 9(5) the court may order that the applicant's costs be paid out of the proceeds of sale` MEANS
    IF `the court makes an order under sub-paragraph (1) or (3)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "On making an order under sub-paragraph (1) or (3)"

-- (1): the proceeds, less the costs of the sale, are paid into court.
-- src:18894 | 10 (1) If a relevant interest is sold in pursuance of an order under paragraph 9, the proceeds of the sale, less the costs of the sale, must be paid into court for the benefit of those who are beneficially interested in the relevant interest.
@ref sch 1B para 10(1) Orders for sale (src:18894)
GIVEN `the proceeds of the sale` IS A NUMBER
      `the costs of the sale` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 1B para 10(1) the amount that must be paid into court` MEANS
    `the proceeds of the sale` MINUS `the costs of the sale`

-- src:18895 | (2) A person who is beneficially interested in the relevant interest may apply to the court for the whole or part of those proceeds to be paid to that person.
@ref sch 1B para 10(2) Orders for sale (src:18895)
GIVEN `the person is beneficially interested in the relevant interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1B para 10(2) the person may apply to the court for the whole or part of the proceeds to be paid to the person` MEANS
    IF `the person is beneficially interested in the relevant interest`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who is beneficially interested in the relevant interest may apply"

-- (3): the whole of the proceeds and interest; or, if another was also beneficially interested at the time of the sale,
-- the proportion that the value of the applicant's interest bears to the total value of the relevant interest.
-- src:18896 | (3) On such an application, the court must order the payment to the applicant of—
-- src:18897 | (a) the whole of the proceeds of sale together with any interest on the proceeds, or
-- src:18898 | (b) if another person was also beneficially interested in the relevant interest at the time of the sale, such proportion of the proceeds (and any interest) as the value of the applicant's interest bears to the total value of the relevant interest.
@ref sch 1B para 10(3) Orders for sale (src:18896-18898)
GIVEN `the proceeds of sale paid into court` IS A NUMBER
      `the interest on the proceeds` IS A NUMBER
      `another person was also beneficially interested in the relevant interest at the time of the sale` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the value of the applicant's interest` IS A NUMBER
      `the total value of the relevant interest` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 1B para 10(3) the amount the court must order to be paid to the applicant` MEANS
    IF `another person was also beneficially interested in the relevant interest at the time of the sale`
    THEN (`the proceeds of sale paid into court` PLUS `the interest on the proceeds`) TIMES (`the value of the applicant's interest` DIVIDED BY `the total value of the relevant interest`)
    ELSE `the proceeds of sale paid into court` PLUS `the interest on the proceeds`

-- src:18899 | (4) If the court has ordered under paragraph 9 that the costs (in Scotland, expenses) of an applicant under that paragraph are to be paid out of the proceeds of sale, the applicant is entitled to payment of those costs (or expenses) out of the proceeds before any person receives any part of the proceeds under this paragraph.
@ref sch 1B para 10(4) Orders for sale (src:18899)
GIVEN `the court has ordered under paragraph 9 that the costs of the applicant under that paragraph are to be paid out of the proceeds of sale` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1B para 10(4) the applicant is entitled to payment of those costs out of the proceeds before any person receives any part of the proceeds under paragraph 10` MEANS
    IF `the court has ordered under paragraph 9 that the costs of the applicant under that paragraph are to be paid out of the proceeds of sale`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the court has ordered under paragraph 9 that the costs ... of an applicant under that paragraph are to be paid out of the proceeds of sale"

-- =========================================================================================================
-- Company's power to withdraw restrictions notice (paragraph 11)
-- =========================================================================================================

-- src:18901 | 11 A company that issues a person with a restrictions notice under paragraph 1 must by notice withdraw the restrictions notice if—
-- src:18902 | (a) it is satisfied that there is a valid reason sufficient to justify the person's failure to comply with the notice served under section 790D , 790DA, 790E or 790EA,
-- src:18903 | (b) the notice served under section 790D , 790DA, 790E or 790EA is complied with, or
-- src:18904 | (c) it discovers that the rights of a third party in respect of the relevant interest are being unfairly affected by the restrictions notice.
@ref sch 1B para 11 Company's power to withdraw restrictions notice (src:18901-18904)
GIVEN `the company is satisfied that there is a valid reason sufficient to justify the person's failure to comply with the notice served under section 790D, 790DA, 790E or 790EA` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice served under section 790D, 790DA, 790E or 790EA is complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company discovers that the rights of a third party in respect of the relevant interest are being unfairly affected by the restrictions notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1B para 11 the company must by notice withdraw the restrictions notice` MEANS
    IF       `the company is satisfied that there is a valid reason sufficient to justify the person's failure to comply with the notice served under section 790D, 790DA, 790E or 790EA`
         OR  `the notice served under section 790D, 790DA, 790E or 790EA is complied with`
         OR  `the company discovers that the rights of a third party in respect of the relevant interest are being unfairly affected by the restrictions notice`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company that issues a person with a restrictions notice under paragraph 1 must by notice withdraw the restrictions notice if" (a), (b) or (c) (a failed "if": marginal reading M1)

-- The same duty as a regulative rule: the company (a party the core names) must withdraw the notice. The text gives
-- no time limit and no consequence, so the rule has neither (nothing is invented).
DECLARE `sch 1B para 11 action` IS ONE OF
    `sch 1B para 11 the company withdraws the restrictions notice by notice`

GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `sch 1B para 11 action`
`sch 1B para 11 the company's duty to withdraw the restrictions notice` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `sch 1B para 11 the company withdraws the restrictions notice by notice`

-- =========================================================================================================
-- Supplementary provision (paragraph 12)
-- =========================================================================================================

-- src:18911 | (3) Regulations under this paragraph are subject to negative resolution procedure.
@ref sch 1B para 12(3) Supplementary provision (src:18911)
GIVETH A `s 1288 procedure for regulations or orders`
`sch 1B para 12(3) the procedure for regulations under paragraph 12` MEANS `s 1289 negative resolution procedure`

-- =========================================================================================================
-- The offences of paragraphs 13, 14, 14A and 14B
-- =========================================================================================================

-- src:18913 | 13 (1) A person to whom a notice under section 790D, 790DA, 790E or 790EA is addressed commits an offence if the person fails, without reasonable excuse, to comply with the notice.
@ref sch 1B para 13(1) Offence of failing to comply with notices (src:18913)
GIVEN `a notice under section 790D, 790DA, 790E or 790EA is addressed to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person fails to comply with the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1B para 13(1) the person commits an offence by failing to comply with the notice` MEANS
    IF `a notice under section 790D, 790DA, 790E or 790EA is addressed to the person` AND `the person fails to comply with the notice` AND NOT (`the person has a reasonable excuse`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person to whom a notice under section 790D, 790DA, 790E or 790EA is addressed commits an offence if the person fails, without reasonable excuse, to comply with the notice" (a failed "if": marginal reading M1)

-- src:18914 | (2) Where the person is a legal entity, the offence is also committed by every officer of the entity who is in default.
@ref sch 1B para 13(2) Offence of failing to comply with notices (src:18914)
GIVEN `the person is a legal entity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence of paragraph 13(1) is committed by the entity` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1B para 13(2) the officer of the entity commits an offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person is a legal entity`)
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the person is a legal entity, the offence is also committed by every officer of the entity who is in default" (a failed "where")
        IF `the offence of paragraph 13(1) is committed by the entity` EQUALS JUST FALSE
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the offence is also committed" (there is no offence of the entity)
        IF `the offence of paragraph 13(1) is committed by the entity` EQUALS NOTHING
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the entity commits the offence is not answered
        OTHERWISE `s 1121 the officer is in default`

-- src:18915 | (3) A person guilty of an offence under this paragraph is liable—
-- src:18916 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding two years or a fine (or both);
-- src:18917 | (b) on summary conviction—
-- src:18918 | (i) in England and Wales, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding the general limit in a magistrates’ court or a fine (or both);
-- src:18919 | (ii) in Scotland, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months or a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (or both);
-- src:18920 | (iii) in Northern Ireland, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months or a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (or both).
@ref sch 1B para 13(3) Offence of failing to comply with notices (src:18915-18920)
GIVEN `how the person is convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction`
      `the general limit in a magistrates' court in England and Wales, in months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`sch 1B para 13(3) the penalty for an offence under paragraph 13` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how the person is convicted`
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on conviction on indictment`, JUST (Period OF 2, Years), JUST `a fine without a stated limit`, NOTHING, TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in England and Wales`, JUST (Period OF `the general limit in a magistrates' court in England and Wales, in months`, Months), JUST `a fine without a stated limit`, NOTHING, TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Scotland` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Scotland`, JUST (Period OF 12, Months), JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`, JUST (Period OF 6, Months), JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph distinguishes England and Wales, Scotland and Northern Ireland on summary conviction

-- src:18922 | 14 (1) A person commits an offence if the person fails, without reasonable excuse, to comply with a duty under section 790G, 790H or 790HA.
